{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null,"message":{"content":"{\"p0\":\"A fixed left-anchored vertical-stripe rule: preserve every cell except recolor 7 to 6 when its zero-based column is 0 mod 3. This matches all observed changes. The distinguishing assumption is that the phase is globally fixed at the left border for every grid width.\",\"p1\":\"A three-column tiling rule: divide the grid into complete bands of width three and recolor 7 only in each band\u2019s first column. This agrees on the observed width of 21. The distinguishing assumption is that an incomplete final band is ignored, unlike a simple modulo rule.\",\"p2\":\"A width-aware band-alignment rule: when the width is divisible by three, use first columns 0,3,6,...; otherwise shift the three-column bands so they align with the right edge, recoloring their first columns. It fits the observed 21-column grid but predicts a different phase for other widths.\",\"p3\":\"An input-anchored periodic rule: choose the stripe phase from an anchor feature, such as the top-left nonzero cell; for this example, that anchor selects phase 0, so 7s in columns 0 mod 3 become 6. The distinguishing assumption is that another grid\u2019s anchor could select a different phase.\"}","reasoning_details":[{"data":"gAAAAABqobucA65FPwTuaeWJws5sjSXalDRbsjYq61aCqSipn2mRh-Je_PRdV5sP9Tle9lkG_-mfFv2vuBlr_nfMqB2KvMPs0Et7jtDpMHNCCtsoJBeYstKf1dq9HY7EcA5Y1Ou-600kHcQy3HHFP-teGggJxfKDR-G6B7D3dxTuIWRHejoz_0Q6rwTCfnK6fuyuwkPF0UoCHwVUuJqjHy7a3WfeJG4NALQafSXxvHgKQbXPcQ_4ttxJE41-QhS5e993zDbQRu6-XIrr9nIN8LhzXPoLyA3LPW8tZkNW9u6XxUyVoHxlKdgRgtwDMKbPLN9D-Ks4Vbcnkf10ZN5hJqmS5gbxP2hHSbk75QTo1U9Bqc9gbYaHVDxV_KLd5ZWgDTqqUfEKPt4GPcrQ10qZ6_E152woGeh9FGNP7u8ecVPkY6bw6asufG76vxLKfi3n98PoSOIHjW8eA_flkcPbnRCYoyzKuulYBsmR9tYXIO-6msXZP4PumPda5OUj_6L1UvtrqYOyHE7gHl6dA_ju0RPEoQqXiSArCbwWDzF9-vrBI4NvQV-w5Kodvj15nEC1uRFuRZK2ZjqfS8jF1uAheXShfYLDc1X7krr5BD45kqgB_Ky-RVwoUi__WAXrj4qVZ6NG5VhiCahQJt5Fgbif2XQzp4tIlk_VCWQS5O_F9QovFtEJxpgz1JO3-dKs2bUv-ae